    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c00a5180-46b1-59a1-a2be-5d72d40aa735",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ is the set of all positive real numbers and zero.\n\n- $-\\pi$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $7.5=\\frac{15}{2}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer, since it can be written as $\\frac{15}{2}$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{25}=-5$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-3\\sqrt{3}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $7.5$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
